# Domain overlay for the Aevia view of the rssn Kernel Manifest.
#
# The manifest says what the kernel *is* (operators, rule sets, kernel
# signatures). This file says how Aevia presents it: which operators form a
# domain module, which of them get a curated typed signature, which rich types
# exist, and what is deliberately left out. See `src/domains.rs`.
#
# Directives (one per line, `#` starts a comment):
#   domain  Name | one-line doc
#   family  Name rule_set:glob [rule_set:glob ...]    first match wins
#   mode    Name typed|dynamic       `typed`: every operator needs sig/dynamic/exclude
#   sig     op [as name](p: T, ...) -> Result<R, OpError>
#   codec   Type to_fn from_fn       wire conversion of a rich type (see prelude)
#   exclude op [op ...] | reason
#   dynamic op [op ...] | reason     accepted as dynamic on purpose
#   prelude Name                     followed by `| ` lines of Aevia source

domain NumberTheory | Number theory over the integers: divisibility, modular arithmetic, primality, factorisation.
domain Combinatorics | Counting, partitions, permutations as numbers, recurrences.
domain Group | Finite groups and permutation groups, presentations, characters.
domain FiniteField | Finite fields GF(p), GF(2^8), extension fields and polynomial arithmetic over them.
domain Coding | Error-correcting codes and checksums.
domain Crypto | Elliptic curves, ECDH/ECDSA and RSA.
domain Graph | Graphs and graph algorithms.
domain Topology | Simplicial and cubical complexes, homology and persistence.
domain Crystallography | Point groups, crystal systems and molecular symmetry.
domain Chaos | Fractals, iterated maps, dynamical-system orbits and fractal dimensions.
domain Graphics | Quaternions, rigid transforms, curves, meshes and rays.
domain Discrete | Remaining discrete-mathematics operators.
domain LieAlgebra | Lie algebras, root systems, representations and Lie groups.
domain Polynomial | Symbolic polynomials, Groebner bases, real-root isolation, partial fractions.
domain Logic | Propositional logic, SAT, BDDs.
domain GeometricAlgebra | Clifford algebra: multivectors, rotors, products.
domain DifferentialGeometry | Metrics, curvature, differential forms, vector calculus in coordinates.
domain Functional | Inner-product spaces, operators and integral equations.
domain Special | Special functions, symbolic and numerical.
domain Statistics | Distributions, tests and descriptive statistics, symbolic and numerical.
domain Calculus | Symbolic calculus, variational calculus, result verification, and D-finite functions (differential equations, recurrences, decided identities).
domain Elementary | Elementary and complex functions, radicals.
domain Core | Kernel plumbing: term constructors, rewriting, CSE, unit conversion.
domain Numeric | Numerical vectors, matrices and callbacks.
domain LinearAlgebra | Symbolic linear algebra, dense and sparse (exact and symbolic sparse matrices, modular methods).
domain Differential | Ordinary, stochastic and partial differential equations.
domain Physics | Classical and quantum physics formulas.
domain Solving | Equation solving and optimisation.
domain Transforms | Integral and discrete transforms.

family NumberTheory number_theory:*
family Combinatorics combinatorics:*
family Group discrete:perm_* discrete:group* discrete:cyclic_group discrete:dihedral_group discrete:symmetric_group discrete:klein_four_group discrete:fp_group* discrete:todd_coxeter* discrete:presentation_* discrete:representation_* discrete:character_*
family FiniteField discrete:gf_* discrete:gfp_* discrete:gfx_* discrete:gf256_* discrete:factor_mod discrete:is_irreducible_mod
family Coding discrete:bch_* discrete:hamming_* discrete:rs_* discrete:crc* discrete:conv_encode discrete:interleave discrete:deinterleave discrete:code_*
family Crypto discrete:ec_* discrete:ecdh_* discrete:ecdsa_* discrete:rsa_*
family Graph discrete:graph* discrete:digraph discrete:induced_subgraph discrete:algebraic_connectivity
family Topology discrete:sc_* discrete:cubical_* discrete:persist* discrete:rips_* discrete:vietoris_* discrete:betti_at_radius discrete:bottleneck_distance
family Crystallography discrete:point_group* discrete:crystal* discrete:bravais_lattices discrete:molecule_*
family Chaos discrete:mandelbrot_* discrete:julia_escape discrete:burning_ship_escape discrete:multibrot_escape discrete:newton_fractal_root discrete:henon_orbit discrete:ifs_* discrete:lorenz* discrete:logistic_* discrete:rossler_orbit discrete:tinkerbell_orbit discrete:map_* discrete:complex_map_* discrete:lyapunov_exponent discrete:orbit_* discrete:moran_dimension discrete:similarity_dimension discrete:box_counting discrete:correlation_dimension
family Graphics discrete:quat_* discrete:rotation_* discrete:translation discrete:translation_* discrete:scaling discrete:scaling_* discrete:shear discrete:shear_* discrete:rotation discrete:reflection discrete:reflection_* discrete:reflect discrete:refract discrete:look_at discrete:perspective discrete:orthographic discrete:ray_* discrete:mesh_* discrete:bezier* discrete:bspline discrete:catmull_rom discrete:barycentric
family Discrete discrete:*
family LieAlgebra lie_structure:* lie:*
family Polynomial poly:*
family Logic logic:*
family GeometricAlgebra geometric_algebra:*
family DifferentialGeometry geometry:*
family Functional functional:*
family Special special:* numerical_special:*
family Statistics stats:* numerical_stats:*
family Calculus calculus:* variational:* verify:* holonomic:*
family Elementary elementary:* complex:* radicals:*
family Core kernel:* rewriting:* cse:* units:*
family Numeric numeric:* numerical_matrix:* numerical_vector:* numerical_callback:*
family LinearAlgebra linalg:* sparse_symbolic:*
family Differential ode:* sde:* pde:*
family Physics physics:* physics_quantum:*
family Solving solve:* optimize:*
family Transforms transforms:*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Typed domains. `mode typed`: a new kernel operator in these families fails
# the coverage test until it is given a `sig`, `dynamic` or `exclude` line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mode NumberTheory typed
mode Combinatorics typed
mode FiniteField typed

# A `sig` is also the overlay's statement that the operator is a pure,
# dimensionless function of its (dimensionless) arguments; see
# `Kernel::call_with_witnesses`. An argument outside an operator's domain comes
# back from the kernel as the unreduced call (`invmod(6, 15)`); the generated
# wrapper turns that into `Err(NotReduced(..))`.

# --- NumberTheory -----------------------------------------------------------
sig gcd(a: Int, b: Int) -> Result<Int, OpError>
sig lcm(a: Int, b: Int) -> Result<Int, OpError>
sig mod as modulo(a: Int, m: Int) -> Result<Int, OpError>
