dynamic period | argument is a rational or a sequence term, no integer-only form
exclude expand_binomial gf_coeffs inclusion_exclusion rsolve | symbolic: they take and return expression terms; call Rssn.dynamic with Real terms
exclude hook_lengths partition_list | ragged results (a list of lists); use Rssn.dynamic and from_value<Tensor<1, Tensor<1, Int>>>

# --- FiniteField ------------------------------------------------------------
# Polynomials are coefficient tensors, highest degree first, residues in [0, p).
sig gf_add(a: Int, b: Int, p: Int) -> Result<Int, OpError>
sig gf_sub(a: Int, b: Int, p: Int) -> Result<Int, OpError>
sig gf_mul(a: Int, b: Int, p: Int) -> Result<Int, OpError>
